<!--
  Removes the built-in `default` user. The ClickHouse package creates it with
  an empty password and no network limit, and a noninteractive install never
  asks for one, so anything that could reach port 8123 or 9000 could run SQL
  as an administrator without credentials.

  Nothing here signs in as `default`: every client names its own user, ON
  CLUSTER statements run through the Keeper queue, and replicas fetch parts
  over the interserver port. The `default` settings profile and quota are
  separate objects and stay.

  The cluster in tr-cluster.xml names no user, so clusterAllReplicas() and
  cluster() would sign in to the other replicas as `default` and are refused
  once it is gone. Ask each node itself, as clickhouse_replicated_migrate.sh
  does.
-->
<clickhouse>
  <users>
    <default remove="remove"/>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
